{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>One important limit, stated up front: because of how state licensing works, we can only see clients who are physically located in California. You can be anywhere in the state, from a home office in Sacramento to a kitchen table in San Diego, but if you've moved out of California, we're not able to continue care across the state line. It isn't a preference, it's the law we practice under, and we take it seriously.</p>
  <p>If you're wondering whether online therapy is a real, lasting option or just a leftover from the pandemic, it's worth knowing that California has made telehealth a permanent, first-class part of how care is delivered here, not a temporary workaround. That's part of why we treat it as the same care rather than a lesser substitute. And research has consistently found video therapy about as effective as meeting in person for most people. What matters most, the relationship and the work, comes through the screen intact.</p>
  <p>Whoever you meet with online is part of the same team Kay trains and supervises. If you'd like to see who you might be working with, <a href="/about/our-team">meet the team</a>.</p>
{% endcall %}
